Build review rounds 1 and 2 (ci/W-468-review-1.log #1, ci/W-468-review-2.log #1) failed on one class, review×fail-open-on-malformed-records-patched-per-site: `staleCitedReds` read a cited red's `# at:` first with the permissive `instant`, then with a pattern of its own that took any fraction of 1-9 digits. The ruling closes the class, not the instance: an exact `# at:` is the studio's one exact UTC profile, `utcTimestampProblem` (opus-model.ts:73 `UTC_PROFILE`, anchored, a fraction of exactly three digits or none, fields in range; opus-model.ts:132 a real Gregorian day, not year 0000), the profile `red`'s `--now` is admitted by and `ladder.ticket` reads red logs by; `red` writes `now.toISOString()` (lifecycle.ts:1183), inside it. `exactInstant` becomes `utcTimestampProblem(v) === undefined ? instant(v)?.getTime() : undefined`, ladder-ticket.ts:52's shape, so no reader keeps a pattern of its own for a later round to find a variant in. Every other form is stale; the no-fraction form, which `red` never writes, is exact by the shared profile, a stated limit (brief:60).

